# waggle-wake — box-local secrets. Copy to waggle-wake.env (gitignored) and fill.
#
# The agent identity whose sealed mail this watches. It must be able to DECRYPT, because a
# NIP-59 sender is inside the seal — there is no way to learn who wrote without opening it.
# That is why this component holds a key at all, and why it belongs on the host that already
# holds agent keys under SOPS rather than on the bridge, which is deliberately keyless.
NVOY_NSEC=

# Whose signature counts as policy. Only these keys' signed grants can authorise a wake.
# Leaving it unset falls back to the maintainer's key; setting it explicitly is better.
#GRANTORS=

# Relays to watch. Defaults to the public trio plus ditto.
#NVOY_RELAYS=wss://relay.damus.io,wss://nos.lol,wss://relay.primal.net,wss://relay.ditto.pub
